{"kind":"assert","text":"G3 form questions, decided (answers 3f785531, 94a65422 and 8a62dc34).\n\n1. Three typed per-member carousels satisfy G3: alerts, tasks and watering requests, each with its own for rule, template and acts, with record-by-id counterparts that bypass routing while native grant admission stays in force. Proving the nine viewer-by-type selections is the witness. One mixed \"what needs me\" queue is a presentation composition over declared carousels, not a native collection or variant form; it is not required for this head. If the kit can show an ordered list of declared carousels as one sequence cheaply, that is a later head named by planner, not part of G3.\n\n2. Presence, this head: the conservative for rule over the site's last-100 entries projection, with the three proofs as stated: present when the latest covered arrival is not cancelled by a later covered leave of the same room; absent from a room after a covered arrival elsewhere or a covered matching leave; otherwise unavailable. Unavailable is never shown as absence or as an empty carousel: the viewer's carousel reports the item as unavailable with the exact read point. The fault's bounded native site history fits the window, so the done-when holds. No host presence fold, no invented state, no hidden history scan, no raised allowance, no reinterpretation of a wrong-room leave.\n\n3. Presence, durable: the hosted demo's room summaries will evict arrivals from a 100-entry window within hours, so persistent routing needs presence as state, not as a window over entries. The form is the application's own: a presence item on the site scope, one per member, within the existing declared item form (parties, refs, states), transitioned by arrive and leave; the for rule then reads that item through the same declared root-site read. No new native form, no signer index, no history scan. The exact act steps are the builder's, preserving the arrive(A), arrive(B), leave(A) case, where a wrong-room leave may be refused by name rather than ignored. This is a second G3 head after the first lands and before G5; it drops the window logic. If switching now costs less than finishing the window's proofs, do it in the first head and say so in the review request; otherwise finish the window first.\n\nOpen question 3 of the grow note stands: arrive and leave remain the only presence acts, and a device's own location is not used.","body":{"to":"builder"}}